gAtoms -- bundled igraph C 1.0.1: vendor compiler-warning cleanup

Target:   src/igraph/vendor/f2c/ and src/igraph/vendor/lapack/
Base:     official igraph 1.0.1 release sources, unmodified
Apply:    from the gAtoms package root,
          patch -p1 < tools/patches/igraph-1.0.1-f2c-cran-warnings.patch

Purpose:  let `R CMD check --as-cran` pass without a compilation WARNING.
          R's check treats any ': warning: suggest parentheses around ...'
          and any ': warning: ... [-Wpointer-to-int-cast]' diagnostic as a
          significant warning and fails the package on it. The pristine
          igraph 1.0.1 sources emit 101 such diagnostics across 37 files
          (56 '&&' within '||', 44 arithmetic/relational operands of a
          shift or bitwise operator, 1 pointer-to-int cast).

Contents: parentheses-only edits, plus one pointer-width cast in signal_.c.
          No algorithm, numerical result, control flow, API or object
          manifest is changed. No -Wno-* flag and no #pragma GCC diagnostic
          is used; nothing is silenced rather than fixed.

The applied state is what src/igraph/ in this repository already contains;
this patch exists so the change is reviewable and replayable.

